Z||000000||olliver||11-01-2001||12:12 AM||||I was just visiting your website.  First of all very nice piece of machinery you have.  I just have one question.  Can you please explain to me the benefits of shaving your intake manifold 1.25".  I have absolutely no idea how that could possibly increase performance.  But i will give you the benefit of the doubt.  I could quite possibly be mistaken, you could have simply done that for some other reason.<P>Thanks,<BR>Olliver||||reg||1
Z||000001||olliver||11-01-2001||08:41 AM||||can anybody tell me reasons why someone would shave their intake manifolds?||||reg||1
Z||000002||1FST2M6||11-01-2001||08:51 AM||||velocity... with the larger intake yeah there is more static volume there but under nitrous that volume creates a problem the fuel tends to seperate and can cause a back fire with as much as i'm fueling.. the smaller runners and lower static volume increase the velocity in the pelenum which evacuates the system faster.. yeah i've lost a bit of torque but gained like 3hp (n/a) but on the spray like 7hp. kind working backwards but it worked... it was spawned by an idea of Shaun41178s and it actually worked!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  ||||reg||1
